viewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Notes","title":"API key rotation and scope management"}},{"document":"Title: Understanding your invoice and usage breakdown\nApplies to: All plans\nSection: Symptoms\n\n- The invoice is higher than expected\n- Charges appear for a service that is not in use\n- The billing period does not align with the calendar month","id":"DOC-BILL-001:91570e0ea364:0","metadata":{"applies_to":"All plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"billing","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":0,"content_sha256":"91570e0ea3642fda5f3ab8e9e48adb7899d27947c4ee23bac8ce1a11cb6be878","doc_id":"DOC-BILL-001","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Symptoms","title":"Understanding your invoice and usage breakdown"}},{"document":"Title: Understanding your invoice and usage breakdown\nApplies to: All plans\nSection: Common causes\n\n- Usage-based charges accrued beyond the plan allowance\n- A resource was left running in a non-production environment\n- The billing period runs from the subscription date rather than the first of the month","id":"DOC-BILL-001:91570e0ea364:1","metadata":{"applies_to":"All plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"billing","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":1,"content_sha256":"91570e0ea3642fda5f3ab8e9e48adb7899d27947c4ee23bac8ce1a11cb6be878","doc_id":"DOC-BILL-001","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Common causes","title":"Understanding your invoice and usage breakdown"}},{"document":"Title: Understanding your invoice and usage breakdown\nApplies to: All plans\nSection: Resolution\n\n1. Open the usage breakdown for the period, which itemises charges by service and by environment.\n2. Look for resources in staging or development environments, which are billed at the same rate as production.\n3. Check the billing period dates at the top of the invoice. The period runs from the anniversary of the subscription date.\n4. Set a usage alert on the billing page so that unexpected accrual is noticed during the period rather than at the end of it.","id":"DOC-BILL-001:91570e0ea364:2","metadata":{"applies_to":"All plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"billing","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":2,"content_sha256":"91570e0ea3642fda5f3ab8e9e48adb7899d27947c4ee23bac8ce1a11cb6be878","doc_id":"DOC-BILL-001","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Resolution","title":"Understanding your invoice and usage breakdown"}},{"document":"Title: Understanding your invoice and usage breakdown\nApplies to: All plans\nSection: Notes\n\nInvoices are finalised three days after the period ends. Adjustments requested before finalisation appear on the same invoice.","id":"DOC-BILL-001:91570e0ea364:3","metadata":{"applies_to":"All plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"billing","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":3,"content_sha256":"91570e0ea3642fda5f3ab8e9e48adb7899d27947c4ee23bac8ce1a11cb6be878","doc_id":"DOC-BILL-001","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Notes","title":"Understanding your invoice and usage breakdown"}},{"document":"Title: Changing plans, and how proration is calculated\nApplies to: All plans\nSection: Symptoms\n\n- The charge after an upgrade differs from the advertised price\n- A downgrade did not take effect immediately\n- A credit is expected but not visible","id":"DOC-BILL-002:dd49cb509f02:0","metadata":{"applies_to":"All plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"billing","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":0,"content_sha256":"dd49cb509f02c542042654f2b2b47e6a3cfd202fd3af9bf09ce9d1306514dda3","doc_id":"DOC-BILL-002","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Symptoms","title":"Changing plans, and how proration is calculated"}},{"document":"Title: Changing plans, and how proration is calculated\nApplies to: All plans\nSection: Common causes\n\n- The upgrade was prorated across the remainder of the billing period\n- Downgrades are applied at the end of the current period rather than immediately\n- The credit was applied to the next invoice rather than refunded","id":"DOC-BILL-002:dd49cb509f02:1","metadata":{"applies_to":"All plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"billing","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":1,"content_sha256":"dd49cb509f02c542042654f2b2b47e6a3cfd202fd3af9bf09ce9d1306514dda3","doc_id":"DOC-BILL-002","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Common causes","title":"Changing plans, and how proration is calculated"}},{"document":"Title: Changing plans, and how proration is calculated\nApplies to: All plans\nSection: Resolution\n\n1. Upgrades take effect immediately and are prorated for the days remaining in the period. The invoice shows the calculation as a separate line.\n2. Downgrades take effect at the start of the next period so that paid-for capacity is not lost. The scheduled change appears on the subscription page.\n3. Credits from a downgrade or an adjustment are applied against the next invoice by default rather than refunded to the payment method.\n4. Where a refund rather than a credit is required, an account owner should raise the request within thirty days of the invoice.","id":"DOC-BILL-002:dd49cb509f02:2","metadata":{"applies_to":"All plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"billing","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":2,"content_sha256":"dd49cb509f02c542042654f2b2b47e6a3cfd202fd3af9bf09ce9d1306514dda3","doc_id":"DOC-BILL-002","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Resolution","title":"Changing plans, and how proration is calculated"}},{"document":"Title: Changing plans, and how proration is calculated\nApplies to: All plans\nSection: Notes\n\nAnnual plans cannot be downgraded mid-term, but capacity can be reduced with effect from the renewal date.","id":"DOC-BILL-002:dd49cb509f02:3","metadata":{"applies_to":"All plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"billing","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":3,"content_sha256":"dd49cb509f02c542042654f2b2b47e6a3cfd202fd3af9bf09ce9d1306514dda3","doc_id":"DOC-BILL-002","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Notes","title":"Changing plans, and how proration is calculated"}},{"document":"Title: Usage limits, overage and spend controls\nApplies to: All plans\nSection: Symptoms\n\n- Service was throttled after a traffic increase\n- Overage charges appeared unexpectedly\n- A spend cap stopped a production workload","id":"DOC-BILL-003:d81849b19a51:0","metadata":{"applies_to":"All plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"billing","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":0,"content_sha256":"d81849b19a51651d65fb2a058fe94a1d72f198345eb34e28c94011b67672fce4","doc_id":"DOC-BILL-003","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Symptoms","title":"Usage limits, overage and spend controls"}},{"document":"Title: Usage limits, overage and spend controls\nApplies to: All plans\nSection: Common causes\n\n- Plan allowance was consumed before the end of the period\n- A spend cap was configured and reached\n- Overage protection is disabled, so usage continued beyond the allowance","id":"DOC-BILL-003:d81849b19a51:1","metadata":{"applies_to":"All plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"billing","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":1,"content_sha256":"d81849b19a51651d65fb2a058fe94a1d72f198345eb34e28c94011b67672fce4","doc_id":"DOC-BILL-003","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Common causes","title":"Usage limits, overage and spend controls"}},{"document":"Title: Usage limits, overage and spend controls\nApplies to: All plans\nSection: Resolution\n\n1. Check the current period usage against the plan allowance on the billing page.\n2. Decide deliberately between a hard spend cap, which stops the service, and overage, which continues at the listed rate. Production workloads generally need the second.\n3. Configure alerts at fifty, eighty and ninety-five per cent of allowance rather than relying on the cap as a warning.\n4. Where a cap has stopped a production service, an account owner can raise it immediately from the billing page and service resumes within a minute.","id":"DOC-BILL-003:d81849b19a51:2","metadata":{"applies_to":"All plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"billing","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":2,"content_sha256":"d81849b19a51651d65fb2a058fe94a1d72f198345eb34e28c94011b67672fce4","doc_id":"DOC-BILL-003","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Resolution","title":"Usage limits, overage and spend controls"}},{"document":"Title: Usage limits, overage and spend controls\nApplies to: All plans\nSection: Notes\n\nSpend caps apply per organisation and cannot currently be set per project.","id":"DOC-BILL-003:d81849b19a51:3","metadata":{"applies_to":"All plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"billing","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":3,"content_sha256":"d81849b19a51651d65fb2a058fe94a1d72f198345eb34e28c94011b67672fce4","doc_id":"DOC-BILL-003","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Notes","title":"Usage limits, overage and spend controls"}},{"document":"Title: Exporting account data and scheduled extracts\nApplies to: All plans\nSection: Symptoms\n\n- An export has not completed\n- The download link has expired\n- The export is missing recent records","id":"DOC-DATA-001:7723dec780de:0","metadata":{"applies_to":"All plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"data","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":0,"content_sha256":"7723dec780deccc3d0d703ac4af09cbdffd7a68550de16a347abf4dc14e3c2fa","doc_id":"DOC-DATA-001","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Symptoms","title":"Exporting account data and scheduled extracts"}},{"document":"Title: Exporting account data and scheduled extracts\nApplies to: All plans\nSection: Common causes\n\n- Large exports are queued and processed asynchronously\n- Download links are valid for twenty-four hours\n- The export captured a snapshot taken when the job started","id":"DOC-DATA-001:7723dec780de:1","metadata":{"applies_to":"All plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"data","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":1,"content_sha256":"7723dec780deccc3d0d703ac4af09cbdffd7a68550de16a347abf4dc14e3c2fa","doc_id":"DOC-DATA-001","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Common causes","title":"Exporting account data and scheduled extracts"}},{"document":"Title: Exporting account data and scheduled extracts\nApplies to: All plans\nSection: Resolution\n\n1. Check the exports page for job status. Jobs covering more than a million records commonly take several minutes.\n2. Request a fresh link from the exports page if the original has expired. The underlying file is retained for seven days.\n3. Note that the export reflects the moment the job began, so records created during processing are not included.\n4. For recurring needs, configure a scheduled export delivered to object storage rather than generating them manually.","id":"DOC-DATA-001:7723dec780de:2","metadata":{"applies_to":"All plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"data","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":2,"content_sha256":"7723dec780deccc3d0d703ac4af09cbdffd7a68550de16a347abf4dc14e3c2fa","doc_id":"DOC-DATA-001","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Resolution","title":"Exporting account data and scheduled extracts"}},{"document":"Title: Exporting account data and scheduled extracts\nApplies to: All plans\nSection: Notes\n\nExports containing personal data are logged in the audit trail with the requesting user and the fields included.","id":"DOC-DATA-001:7723dec780de:3","metadata":{"applies_to":"All plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"data","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":3,"content_sha256":"7723dec780deccc3d0d703ac4af09cbdffd7a68550de16a347abf4dc14e3c2fa","doc_id":"DOC-DATA-001","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Notes","title":"Exporting account data and scheduled extracts"}},{"document":"Title: Backups, retention and point-in-time restore\nApplies to: Managed Database\nSection: Symptoms\n\n- Data was deleted and needs recovering\n- A restore is taking longer than expected\n- A backup is older than expected","id":"DOC-DATA-002:a8bdc1b80ab6:0","metadata":{"applies_to":"Managed Database","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"data","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":0,"content_sha256":"a8bdc1b80ab6fac76dbfdea1337fa44d148c3f8d1cda83d476ee18a7dbb78c2c","doc_id":"DOC-DATA-002","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Symptoms","title":"Backups, retention and point-in-time restore"}},{"document":"Title: Backups, retention and point-in-time restore\nApplies to: Managed Database\nSection: Common causes\n\n- Automated backups run daily and retention depends on the plan\n- Restore time scales with database size\n- Point-in-time recovery is available only where continuous archiving is enabled","id":"DOC-DATA-002:a8bdc1b80ab6:1","metadata":{"applies_to":"Managed Database","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"data","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":1,"content_sha256":"a8bdc1b80ab6fac76dbfdea1337fa44d148c3f8d1cda83d476ee18a7dbb78c2c","doc_id":"DOC-DATA-002","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Common causes","title":"Backups, retention and point-in-time restore"}},{"document":"Title: Backups, retention and point-in-time restore\nApplies to: Managed Database\nSection: Resolution\n\n1. Identify the point you need to restore to. Point-in-time recovery covers any moment within the retention window rather than only backup times.\n2. Restore into a new database instance rather than over the existing one, so the current state is preserved while you verify the restore.\n3. Allow roughly ten minutes per hundred gigabytes for the restore, and considerably longer where the instance is also under load.\n4. Verify the restored data before switching traffic, and keep the original instance until that verification is complete.","id":"DOC-DATA-002:a8bdc1b80ab6:2","metadata":{"applies_to":"Managed Database","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"data","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":2,"content_sha256":"a8bdc1b80ab6fac76dbfdea1337fa44d148c3f8d1cda83d476ee18a7dbb78c2c","doc_id":"DOC-DATA-002","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Resolution","title":"Backups, retention and point-in-time restore"}},{"document":"Title: Backups, retention and point-in-time restore\nApplies to: Managed Database\nSection: Notes\n\nRetention is seven days on Standard, thirty days on Business and ninety days on Enterprise plans.","id":"DOC-DATA-002:a8bdc1b80ab6:3","metadata":{"applies_to":"Managed Database","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"data","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":3,"content_sha256":"a8bdc1b80ab6fac76dbfdea1337fa44d148c3f8d1cda83d476ee18a7dbb78c2c","doc_id":"DOC-DATA-002","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Notes","title":"Backups, retention and point-in-time restore"}},{"document":"Title: Data residency and regional storage\nApplies to: Business and Enterprise plans\nSection: Symptoms\n\n- A customer requires data to remain in a specific region\n- Latency is high for users far from the primary region\n- A compliance review has asked where data is held","id":"DOC-DATA-003:4191397fcaef:0","metadata":{"applies_to":"Business and Enterprise plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"data","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":0,"content_sha256":"4191397fcaef14f0afd0f0ad93e07c28d9e71fd15047dd655643bb203041307a","doc_id":"DOC-DATA-003","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Symptoms","title":"Data residency and regional storage"}},{"document":"Title: Data residency and regional storage\nApplies to: Business and Enterprise plans\nSection: Common causes\n\n- The organisation was created in a region that no longer suits the requirement\n- Read traffic is being served from the primary region only\n- Backups are replicated to a second region by default","id":"DOC-DATA-003:4191397fcaef:1","metadata":{"applies_to":"Business and Enterprise plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"data","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":1,"content_sha256":"4191397fcaef14f0afd0f0ad93e07c28d9e71fd15047dd655643bb203041307a","doc_id":"DOC-DATA-003","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Common causes","title":"Data residency and regional storage"}},{"document":"Title: Data residency and regional storage\nApplies to: Business and Enterprise plans\nSection: Resolution\n\n1. Check the region shown on the organisation settings page. This is fixed at creation and determines where primary data is stored.\n2. Enable read replicas in additional regions to reduce latency for distant users without moving primary storage.\n3. Review the backup replication setting if a single-region requirement applies, since cross-region replication is enabled by default.\n4. Migrating an organisation between regions requires a planned migration with support and involves a maintenance window.","id":"DOC-DATA-003:4191397fcaef:2","metadata":{"applies_to":"Business and Enterprise plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"data","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":2,"content_sha256":"4191397fcaef14f0afd0f0ad93e07c28d9e71fd15047dd655643bb203041307a","doc_id":"DOC-DATA-003","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Resolution","title":"Data residency and regional storage"}},{"document":"Title: Data residency and regional storage\nApplies to: Business and Enterprise plans\nSection: Notes\n\nMetadata such as account names and billing records is stored centrally regardless of the data region.","id":"DOC-DATA-003:4191397fcaef:3","metadata":{"applies_to":"Business and Enterprise plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"data","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":3,"content_sha256":"4191397fcaef14f0afd0f0ad93e07c28d9e71fd15047dd655643bb203041307a","doc_id":"DOC-DATA-003","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Notes","title":"Data residency and regional storage"}},{"document":"Title: Container deployments failing during the health check phase\nApplies to: Container Service\nSection: Symptoms\n\n- The deployment reaches running and then rolls back\n- Logs show repeated health check timeouts\n- The service works locally but not when deployed","id":"DOC-DEPLOY-001:8803954669e7:0","metadata":{"applies_to":"Container Service","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"deployment","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":0,"content_sha256":"8803954669e77b39d2102c153e6136b24b148acc97aad31df49fc1637d2f0ea5","doc_id":"DOC-DEPLOY-001","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Symptoms","title":"Container deployments failing during the health check phase"}},{"document":"Title: Container deployments failing during the health check phase\nApplies to: Container Service\nSection: Common causes\n\n- The health endpoint takes longer to respond than the configured timeout\n- The container listens on a different port than the service declares\n- A required environment variable is absent in the deployed environment","id":"DOC-DEPLOY-001:8803954669e7:1","metadata":{"applies_to":"Container Service","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"deployment","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":1,"content_sha256":"8803954669e77b39d2102c153e6136b24b148acc97aad31df49fc1637d2f0ea5","doc_id":"DOC-DEPLOY-001","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Common causes","title":"Container deployments failing during the health check phase"}},{"document":"Title: Container deployments failing during the health check phase\nApplies to: Container Service\nSection: Resolution\n\n1. Confirm the container is listening on the port declared in the service definition. A mismatch here produces a health check failure that looks like a timeout.\n2. Increase the initial delay if the application needs time to warm up before it can answer. Thirty seconds is a reasonable starting point for services that load models or caches.\n3. Compare the environment variables present in the deployment against those the application requires. Missing configuration frequently causes a silent startup failure.\n4. Inspect the container logs from the failed revision rather than the running one; the rollback replaces the logs shown by default.","id":"DOC-DEPLOY-001:8803954669e7:2","metadata":{"applies_to":"Container Service","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"deployment","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":2,"content_sha256":"8803954669e77b39d2102c153e6136b24b148acc97aad31df49fc1637d2f0ea5","doc_id":"DOC-DEPLOY-001","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Resolution","title":"Container deployments failing during the health check phase"}},{"document":"Title: Container deployments failing during the health check phase\nApplies to: Container Service\nSection: Notes\n\nA health check must return within the timeout using only local state. Endpoints that call a database will fail during a database incident and take the service down with them.","id":"DOC-DEPLOY-001:8803954669e7:3","metadata":{"applies_to":"Container Service","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"deployment","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":3,"content_sha256":"8803954669e77b39d2102c153e6136b24b148acc97aad31df49fc1637d2f0ea5","doc_id":"DOC-DEPLOY-001","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Notes","title":"Container deployments failing during the health check phase"}},{"document":"Title: Rolling back a failed release\nApplies to: Container Service, Functions\nSection: Symptoms\n\n- A release has introduced errors and must be reverted\n- The previous revision is needed while a fix is prepared","id":"DOC-DEPLOY-002:5fe22bc65f84:0","metadata":{"applies_to":"Container Service, Functions","approval_status":"expired","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"deployment","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":0,"content_sha256":"5fe22bc65f842d3ff66171447298973b774cee9ab84b6f1ad7b93edae7f31d8c","doc_id":"DOC-DEPLOY-002","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Symptoms","title":"Rolling back a failed release"}},{"document":"Title: Rolling back a failed release\nApplies to: Container Service, Functions\nSection: Common causes\n\n- A defect reached production that testing did not catch\n- A configuration change had unintended effects","id":"DOC-DEPLOY-002:5fe22bc65f84:1","metadata":{"applies_to":"Container Service, Functions","approval_status":"expired","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"deployment","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":1,"content_sha256":"5fe22bc65f842d3ff66171447298973b774cee9ab84b6f1ad7b93edae7f31d8c","doc_id":"DOC-DEPLOY-002","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Common causes","title":"Rolling back a failed release"}},{"document":"Title: Rolling back a failed release\nApplies to: Container Service, Functions\nSection: Resolution\n\n1. Open the revisions page for the service and identify the last revision that was healthy.\n2. Select roll back on that revision. Traffic moves within roughly thirty seconds and no rebuild takes place.\n3. If the release included a database migration, roll the migration back before the service, or the older code will encounter a schema it does not expect.\n4. Record the incident and the reason for the rollback before deploying a fix, while the detail is still fresh.","id":"DOC-DEPLOY-002:5fe22bc65f84:2","metadata":{"applies_to":"Container Service, Functions","approval_status":"expired","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"deployment","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":2,"content_sha256":"5fe22bc65f842d3ff66171447298973b774cee9ab84b6f1ad7b93edae7f31d8c","doc_id":"DOC-DEPLOY-002","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Resolution","title":"Rolling back a failed release"}},{"document":"Title: Rolling back a failed release\nApplies to: Container Service, Functions\nSection: Notes\n\nRollback restores the container image and its configuration together. It does not restore data.","id":"DOC-DEPLOY-002:5fe22bc65f84:3","metadata":{"applies_to":"Container Service, Functions","approval_status":"expired","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"deployment","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":3,"content_sha256":"5fe22bc65f842d3ff66171447298973b774cee9ab84b6f1ad7b93edae7f31d8c","doc_id":"DOC-DEPLOY-002","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Notes","title":"Rolling back a failed release"}},{"document":"Title: Build failures caused by dependency resolution\nApplies to: Build Service\nSection: Symptoms\n\n- Builds that previously succeeded now fail without code changes\n- The build works locally but fails in the pipeline\n- Dependency resolution takes far longer than usual","id":"DOC-DEPLOY-003:7403b724b7b2:0","metadata":{"applies_to":"Build Service","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"deployment","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":0,"content_sha256":"7403b724b7b2c2fe0786dfc491f444322b4b274344f781f84d93f334ea581487","doc_id":"DOC-DEPLOY-003","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Symptoms","title":"Build failures caused by dependency resolution"}},{"document":"Title: Build failures caused by dependency resolution\nApplies to: Build Service\nSection: Common causes\n\n- An unpinned dependency released a new incompatible version\n- The build environment uses a different language runtime than the local machine\n- The dependency cache holds a partially written artefact","id":"DOC-DEPLOY-003:7403b724b7b2:1","metadata":{"applies_to":"Build Service","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"deployment","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":1,"content_sha256":"7403b724b7b2c2fe0786dfc491f444322b4b274344f781f84d93f334ea581487","doc_id":"DOC-DEPLOY-003","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Common causes","title":"Build failures caused by dependency resolution"}},{"document":"Title: Build failures caused by dependency resolution\nApplies to: Build Service\nSection: Resolution\n\n1. Pin your dependencies with exact versions and commit the lock file. Unpinned dependencies are the cause in the large majority of cases of this kind.\n2. Compare the runtime version declared in your build configuration against the version you use locally.\n3. Clear the build cache from the settings page and trigger a fresh build to rule out a corrupted artefact.\n4. If a specific dependency is failing to resolve, check whether its registry is reachable from the build network.","id":"DOC-DEPLOY-003:7403b724b7b2:2","metadata":{"applies_to":"Build Service","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"deployment","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":2,"content_sha256":"7403b724b7b2c2fe0786dfc491f444322b4b274344f781f84d93f334ea581487","doc_id":"DOC-DEPLOY-003","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Resolution","title":"Build failures caused by dependency resolution"}},{"document":"Title: Build failures caused by dependency resolution\nApplies to: Build Service\nSection: Notes\n\nBuild logs retain the full resolution output for thirty days, which is usually enough to identify which version changed.","id":"DOC-DEPLOY-003:7403b724b7b2:3","metadata":{"applies_to":"Build Service","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"deployment","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":3,"content_sha256":"7403b724b7b2c2fe0786dfc491f444322b4b274344f781f84d93f334ea581487","doc_id":"DOC-DEPLOY-003","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Notes","title":"Build failures caused by dependency resolution"}},{"document":"Title: Configuring environment variables and secrets\nApplies to: All compute services\nSection: Symptoms\n\n- The application cannot read a variable that appears to be set\n- A secret value appears in plain text in the logs\n- Configuration differs between environments unexpectedly","id":"DOC-DEPLOY-004:9789e12635d2:0","metadata":{"applies_to":"All compute services","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"deployment","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":0,"content_sha256":"9789e12635d2cb8aba531cdb6816e5a0da5774f8a970afd6f09b0a2ff022f39b","doc_id":"DOC-DEPLOY-004","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Symptoms","title":"Configuring environment variables and secrets"}},{"document":"Title: Configuring environment variables and secrets\nApplies to: All compute services\nSection: Common causes\n\n- The variable was set at project scope but read at service scope\n- The application logs its configuration at startup\n- An environment override exists that is not visible on the main settings page","id":"DOC-DEPLOY-004:9789e12635d2:1","metadata":{"applies_to":"All compute services","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"deployment","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":1,"content_sha256":"9789e12635d2cb8aba531cdb6816e5a0da5774f8a970afd6f09b0a2ff022f39b","doc_id":"DOC-DEPLOY-004","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Common causes","title":"Configuring environment variables and secrets"}},{"document":"Title: Configuring environment variables and secrets\nApplies to: All compute services\nSection: Resolution\n\n1. Check the scope at which the variable was defined. Service scope overrides project scope, and project scope overrides organisation defaults.\n2. Store anything sensitive as a secret rather than a variable. Secrets are masked in logs and are not readable through the API after creation.\n3. Review the environment overrides page, which lists values that differ from the defaults for each environment.\n4. Redeploy after changing configuration. Running containers do not pick up new values without a restart.","id":"DOC-DEPLOY-004:9789e12635d2:2","metadata":{"applies_to":"All compute services","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"deployment","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":2,"content_sha256":"9789e12635d2cb8aba531cdb6816e5a0da5774f8a970afd6f09b0a2ff022f39b","doc_id":"DOC-DEPLOY-004","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Resolution","title":"Configuring environment variables and secrets"}},{"document":"Title: Configuring environment variables and secrets\nApplies to: All compute services\nSection: Notes\n\nA secret that has been printed to logs should be treated as exposed and rotated, even if the logs are private.","id":"DOC-DEPLOY-004:9789e12635d2:3","metadata":{"applies_to":"All compute services","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"deployment","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":3,"content_sha256":"9789e12635d2cb8aba531cdb6816e5a0da5774f8a970afd6f09b0a2ff022f39b","doc_id":"DOC-DEPLOY-004","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Notes","title":"Configuring environment variables and secrets"}},{"document":"Title: Connecting continuous integration pipelines\nApplies to: All plans\nSection: Symptoms\n\n- The pipeline cannot authenticate against CloudServe\n- Deployments succeed manually but fail from the pipeline\n- The pipeline has broader access than intended","id":"DOC-INT-001:76bbb5515df0:0","metadata":{"applies_to":"All plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"integration","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":0,"content_sha256":"76bbb5515df02adcd6445c50f7b258c4270bc35655f1752ca4fbde23a8476f4f","doc_id":"DOC-INT-001","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Symptoms","title":"Connecting continuous integration pipelines"}},{"document":"Title: Connecting continuous integration pipelines\nApplies to: All plans\nSection: Common causes\n\n- A personal key was used rather than a service account\n- The pipeline environment lacks the configuration present locally\n- The service account was granted an organisation-wide role","id":"DOC-INT-001:76bbb5515df0:1","metadata":{"applies_to":"All plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"integration","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":1,"content_sha256":"76bbb5515df02adcd6445c50f7b258c4270bc35655f1752ca4fbde23a8476f4f","doc_id":"DOC-INT-001","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Common causes","title":"Connecting continuous integration pipelines"}},{"document":"Title: Connecting continuous integration pipelines\nApplies to: All plans\nSection: Resolution\n\n1. Create a service account for the pipeline rather than using a personal key, so that access survives staff changes.\n2. Grant the service account only the projects and permissions the pipeline needs, and review that grant when the pipeline changes.\n3. Store the credential as an encrypted secret in your pipeline provider, never in the repository.\n4. Test the pipeline credential separately from the deployment logic, so that authentication failures are distinguishable from deployment failures.","id":"DOC-INT-001:76bbb5515df0:2","metadata":{"applies_to":"All plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"integration","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":2,"content_sha256":"76bbb5515df02adcd6445c50f7b258c4270bc35655f1752ca4fbde23a8476f4f","doc_id":"DOC-INT-001","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Resolution","title":"Connecting continuous integration pipelines"}},{"document":"Title: Connecting continuous integration pipelines\nApplies to: All plans\nSection: Notes\n\nService account keys do not expire by default. Set an expiry and rotate on a schedule.","id":"DOC-INT-001:76bbb5515df0:3","metadata":{"applies_to":"All plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"integration","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":3,"content_sha256":"76bbb5515df02adcd6445c50f7b258c4270bc35655f1752ca4fbde23a8476f4f","doc_id":"DOC-INT-001","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Notes","title":"Connecting continuous integration pipelines"}},{"document":"Title: Third party monitoring and log forwarding\nApplies to: Business and Enterprise plans\nSection: Symptoms\n\n- Logs are not arriving at the external destination\n- Metrics are delayed compared with the console\n- Forwarded volume is higher than expected","id":"DOC-INT-002:a0ec300e67d0:0","metadata":{"applies_to":"Business and Enterprise plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"integration","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":0,"content_sha256":"a0ec300e67d07625d98f9aaacbd7255427e5d0abb02194fd8edbc7285094296d","doc_id":"DOC-INT-002","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Symptoms","title":"Third party monitoring and log forwarding"}},{"document":"Title: Third party monitoring and log forwarding\nApplies to: Business and Enterprise plans\nSection: Common causes\n\n- The destination rejected the payload and forwarding paused\n- Aggregation introduces a delay before metrics are forwarded\n- Debug-level logs are being forwarded along with the rest","id":"DOC-INT-002:a0ec300e67d0:1","metadata":{"applies_to":"Business and Enterprise plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"integration","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":1,"content_sha256":"a0ec300e67d07625d98f9aaacbd7255427e5d0abb02194fd8edbc7285094296d","doc_id":"DOC-INT-002","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Common causes","title":"Third party monitoring and log forwarding"}},{"document":"Title: Third party monitoring and log forwarding\nApplies to: Business and Enterprise plans\nSection: Resolution\n\n1. Check the forwarding status page, which shows the last successful delivery and any error returned by the destination.\n2. Expect a delay of up to two minutes on metrics, since they are aggregated before being sent.\n3. Apply a level filter at source so that debug output is not forwarded, which is usually the reason volume is higher than expected.\n4. Verify the destination credential separately if delivery has stopped entirely, as expired credentials are the most common cause.","id":"DOC-INT-002:a0ec300e67d0:2","metadata":{"applies_to":"Business and Enterprise plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"integration","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":2,"content_sha256":"a0ec300e67d07625d98f9aaacbd7255427e5d0abb02194fd8edbc7285094296d","doc_id":"DOC-INT-002","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Resolution","title":"Third party monitoring and log forwarding"}},{"document":"Title: Third party monitoring and log forwarding\nApplies to: Business and Enterprise plans\nSection: Notes\n\nForwarding pauses after one hour of consecutive failures and must be resumed manually once the destination is healthy.","id":"DOC-INT-002:a0ec300e67d0:3","metadata":{"applies_to":"Business and Enterprise plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"integration","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":3,"content_sha256":"a0ec300e67d07625d98f9aaacbd7255427e5d0abb02194fd8edbc7285094296d","doc_id":"DOC-INT-002","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Notes","title":"Third party monitoring and log forwarding"}},{"document":"Title: First deployment: a walkthrough\nApplies to: All plans\nSection: Symptoms\n\n- A new user does not know where to begin\n- The first deployment fails for unclear reasons","id":"DOC-ONB-001:9a29d130e136:0","metadata":{"applies_to":"All plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"onboarding","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":0,"content_sha256":"9a29d130e136b90d3f276439ae8c0b8c1ec7136a6e0d06f7fdd9af9b83ffb7f5","doc_id":"DOC-ONB-001","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Symptoms","title":"First deployment: a walkthrough"}},{"document":"Title: First deployment: a walkthrough\nApplies to: All plans\nSection: Common causes\n\n- Required configuration has not been set\n- The project structure does not match what the build expects","id":"DOC-ONB-001:9a29d130e136:1","metadata":{"applies_to":"All plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"onboarding","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":1,"content_sha256":"9a29d130e136b90d3f276439ae8c0b8c1ec7136a6e0d06f7fdd9af9b83ffb7f5","doc_id":"DOC-ONB-001","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Common causes","title":"First deployment: a walkthrough"}},{"document":"Title: First deployment: a walkthrough\nApplies to: All plans\nSection: Resolution\n\n1. Create a project, then a service within it. Resources belong to services and services belong to projects.\n2. Connect a repository or push a container image. The build service detects common project layouts automatically.\n3. Set any environment variables the application needs before the first deployment rather than after it.\n4. Deploy, then watch the logs for the first sixty seconds. Most first-deployment problems are visible immediately in startup output.","id":"DOC-ONB-001:9a29d130e136:2","metadata":{"applies_to":"All plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"onboarding","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":2,"content_sha256":"9a29d130e136b90d3f276439ae8c0b8c1ec7136a6e0d06f7fdd9af9b83ffb7f5","doc_id":"DOC-ONB-001","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Resolution","title":"First deployment: a walkthrough"}},{"document":"Title: First deployment: a walkthrough\nApplies to: All plans\nSection: Notes\n\nThe free tier includes one service and is sufficient for evaluating the platform.","id":"DOC-ONB-001:9a29d130e136:3","metadata":{"applies_to":"All plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"onboarding","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":3,"content_sha256":"9a29d130e136b90d3f276439ae8c0b8c1ec7136a6e0d06f7fdd9af9b83ffb7f5","doc_id":"DOC-ONB-001","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Notes","title":"First deployment: a walkthrough"}},{"document":"Title: Migrating an existing application to CloudServe\nApplies to: All plans\nSection: Symptoms\n\n- An existing application needs moving with minimal downtime\n- The application depends on services not yet available","id":"DOC-ONB-002:da7894e96187:0","metadata":{"applies_to":"All plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"onboarding","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":0,"content_sha256":"da7894e961871d50c1c9380616e6aa5a11bb9ac0bb3150236c186234b8122d17","doc_id":"DOC-ONB-002","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Symptoms","title":"Migrating an existing application to CloudServe"}},{"document":"Title: Migrating an existing application to CloudServe\nApplies to: All plans\nSection: Common causes\n\n- Configuration is embedded in the application rather than externalised\n- The application depends on local state that will not survive scaling","id":"DOC-ONB-002:da7894e96187:1","metadata":{"applies_to":"All plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"onboarding","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":1,"content_sha256":"da7894e961871d50c1c9380616e6aa5a11bb9ac0bb3150236c186234b8122d17","doc_id":"DOC-ONB-002","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Common causes","title":"Migrating an existing application to CloudServe"}},{"document":"Title: Migrating an existing application to CloudServe\nApplies to: All plans\nSection: Resolution\n\n1. Externalise configuration before migrating. Anything read from a file on disk should move to environment variables or secrets.\n2. Identify local state such as uploaded files or session data and move it to object storage or the managed database first.\n3. Run in parallel with the existing deployment and shift a small share of traffic before committing to the move.\n4. Plan the database migration separately from the application migration; attempting both at once makes any failure hard to diagnose.","id":"DOC-ONB-002:da7894e96187:2","metadata":{"applies_to":"All plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"onboarding","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":2,"content_sha256":"da7894e961871d50c1c9380616e6aa5a11bb9ac0bb3150236c186234b8122d17","doc_id":"DOC-ONB-002","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Resolution","title":"Migrating an existing application to CloudServe"}},{"document":"Title: Migrating an existing application to CloudServe\nApplies to: All plans\nSection: Notes\n\nApplications that write to the local filesystem will lose that data on every deployment and every scaling event.","id":"DOC-ONB-002:da7894e96187:3","metadata":{"applies_to":"All plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"onboarding","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":3,"content_sha256":"da7894e961871d50c1c9380616e6aa5a11bb9ac0bb3150236c186234b8122d17","doc_id":"DOC-ONB-002","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Notes","title":"Migrating an existing application to CloudServe"}},{"document":"Title: Diagnosing elevated response latency\nApplies to: All compute services\nSection: Symptoms\n\n- Response times have increased without a code change\n- The 95th percentile is far above the median\n- Latency rises at predictable times of day","id":"DOC-PERF-001:a98309888a24:0","metadata":{"applies_to":"All compute services","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"performance","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":0,"content_sha256":"a98309888a242063cd5702600ab5b440fc9862a9f096531189f1a75b02cd4c7b","doc_id":"DOC-PERF-001","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Symptoms","title":"Diagnosing elevated response latency"}},{"document":"Title: Diagnosing elevated response latency\nApplies to: All compute services\nSection: Common causes\n\n- The service is running close to its memory limit and spending time in garbage collection\n- A downstream dependency has slowed and the delay is propagating\n- Instance count is not scaling with the load pattern","id":"DOC-PERF-001:a98309888a24:1","metadata":{"applies_to":"All compute services","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"performance","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":1,"content_sha256":"a98309888a242063cd5702600ab5b440fc9862a9f096531189f1a75b02cd4c7b","doc_id":"DOC-PERF-001","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Common causes","title":"Diagnosing elevated response latency"}},{"document":"Title: Diagnosing elevated response latency\nApplies to: All compute services\nSection: Resolution\n\n1. Compare median and 95th percentile latency on the metrics page. A large gap points to contention or queueing rather than a uniformly slower service.\n2. Check memory utilisation across instances. Sustained utilisation above eighty per cent typically shows up as latency before it shows up as failure.\n3. Review the dependency timing breakdown on the trace view to identify whether the time is being spent in your service or waiting on another.\n4. Adjust the autoscaling policy if load is predictable. Scaling on request count responds sooner than scaling on processor utilisation.","id":"DOC-PERF-001:a98309888a24:2","metadata":{"applies_to":"All compute services","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"performance","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":2,"content_sha256":"a98309888a242063cd5702600ab5b440fc9862a9f096531189f1a75b02cd4c7b","doc_id":"DOC-PERF-001","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Resolution","title":"Diagnosing elevated response latency"}},{"document":"Title: Diagnosing elevated response latency\nApplies to: All compute services\nSection: Notes\n\nCold starts affect the first request to a new instance. Frequent scaling events will therefore raise the 95th percentile even when the service itself is healthy.","id":"DOC-PERF-001:a98309888a24:3","metadata":{"applies_to":"All compute services","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"performance","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":3,"content_sha256":"a98309888a242063cd5702600ab5b440fc9862a9f096531189f1a75b02cd4c7b","doc_id":"DOC-PERF-001","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Notes","title":"Diagnosing elevated response latency"}},{"document":"Title: Autoscaling behaviour and instance limits\nApplies to: Container Service\nSection: Symptoms\n\n- The service does not scale up under load\n- Scaling happens later than expected\n- Instance count oscillates","id":"DOC-PERF-002:69a73e6284a6:0","metadata":{"applies_to":"Container Service","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"performance","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":0,"content_sha256":"69a73e6284a6e55670bd7f5ac88f936b8b5565d32d412ab3a48b0742558f265f","doc_id":"DOC-PERF-002","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Symptoms","title":"Autoscaling behaviour and instance limits"}},{"document":"Title: Autoscaling behaviour and instance limits\nApplies to: Container Service\nSection: Common causes\n\n- The maximum instance count has been reached\n- The scaling metric responds more slowly than the load changes\n- The cooldown period is shorter than the time a new instance takes to become ready","id":"DOC-PERF-002:69a73e6284a6:1","metadata":{"applies_to":"Container Service","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"performance","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":1,"content_sha256":"69a73e6284a6e55670bd7f5ac88f936b8b5565d32d412ab3a48b0742558f265f","doc_id":"DOC-PERF-002","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Common causes","title":"Autoscaling behaviour and instance limits"}},{"document":"Title: Autoscaling behaviour and instance limits\nApplies to: Container Service\nSection: Resolution\n\n1. Check whether the service is sitting at its configured maximum. Scaling stops there regardless of load.\n2. Choose a scaling metric that reflects the pressure you actually face. Request concurrency reacts faster than processor utilisation for request-bound services.\n3. Set the cooldown longer than your startup time so that new instances are counted before another scaling decision is taken.\n4. Set a minimum instance count above zero for latency-sensitive services to avoid cold starts on the first request.","id":"DOC-PERF-002:69a73e6284a6:2","metadata":{"applies_to":"Container Service","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"performance","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":2,"content_sha256":"69a73e6284a6e55670bd7f5ac88f936b8b5565d32d412ab3a48b0742558f265f","doc_id":"DOC-PERF-002","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Resolution","title":"Autoscaling behaviour and instance limits"}},{"document":"Title: Autoscaling behaviour and instance limits\nApplies to: Container Service\nSection: Notes\n\nScaling decisions are evaluated every fifteen seconds. Very short traffic spikes will finish before scaling responds.","id":"DOC-PERF-002:69a73e6284a6:3","metadata":{"applies_to":"Container Service","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"performance","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":3,"content_sha256":"69a73e6284a6e55670bd7f5ac88f936b8b5565d32d412ab3a48b0742558f265f","doc_id":"DOC-PERF-002","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Notes","title":"Autoscaling behaviour and instance limits"}},{"document":"Title: Database connection pool exhaustion\nApplies to: Managed Database\nSection: Symptoms\n\n- Errors indicating no connection is available\n- Latency increases sharply as traffic grows\n- The database reports far fewer active queries than the application expects","id":"DOC-PERF-003:739f203ce10d:0","metadata":{"applies_to":"Managed Database","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"performance","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":0,"content_sha256":"739f203ce10dca1990d492286b48ec67c55d00ed8de9b0c7251eb23a2668a466","doc_id":"DOC-PERF-003","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Symptoms","title":"Database connection pool exhaustion"}},{"document":"Title: Database connection pool exhaustion\nApplies to: Managed Database\nSection: Common causes\n\n- The pool size multiplied by the instance count exceeds the database connection limit\n- Connections are not being returned to the pool after use\n- Long-running transactions are holding connections open","id":"DOC-PERF-003:739f203ce10d:1","metadata":{"applies_to":"Managed Database","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"performance","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":1,"content_sha256":"739f203ce10dca1990d492286b48ec67c55d00ed8de9b0c7251eb23a2668a466","doc_id":"DOC-PERF-003","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Common causes","title":"Database connection pool exhaustion"}},{"document":"Title: Database connection pool exhaustion\nApplies to: Managed Database\nSection: Resolution\n\n1. Calculate the total possible connections as pool size multiplied by maximum instances, and compare it against your plan's connection limit.\n2. Reduce the per-instance pool size rather than raising the limit. A large number of small pools is usually the wrong shape for a scaled service.\n3. Look for queries that hold a transaction open across a network call to another service, which is the most common cause of leaks of this kind.\n4. Consider a connection proxy if the instance count must remain high, so that pooling happens once rather than per instance.","id":"DOC-PERF-003:739f203ce10d:2","metadata":{"applies_to":"Managed Database","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"performance","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":2,"content_sha256":"739f203ce10dca1990d492286b48ec67c55d00ed8de9b0c7251eb23a2668a466","doc_id":"DOC-PERF-003","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Resolution","title":"Database connection pool exhaustion"}},{"document":"Title: Database connection pool exhaustion\nApplies to: Managed Database\nSection: Notes\n\nThe connection limit is a property of the database plan and is listed on the plan comparison page.","id":"DOC-PERF-003:739f203ce10d:3","metadata":{"applies_to":"Managed Database","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"performance","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":3,"content_sha256":"739f203ce10dca1990d492286b48ec67c55d00ed8de9b0c7251eb23a2668a466","doc_id":"DOC-PERF-003","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Notes","title":"Database connection pool exhaustion"}},{"document":"Title: Responding to a suspected account compromise\nApplies to: All plans\nSection: Symptoms\n\n- Unrecognised activity appears in the audit log\n- A user reports credentials may have been exposed\n- Resources were created that nobody claims","id":"DOC-SEC-001:50fa532aa23b:0","metadata":{"applies_to":"All plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"security","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":0,"content_sha256":"50fa532aa23b932d2aa7250a85eb6d758f9a997bd4a063301b133d4081453a67","doc_id":"DOC-SEC-001","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Symptoms","title":"Responding to a suspected account compromise"}},{"document":"Title: Responding to a suspected account compromise\nApplies to: All plans\nSection: Common causes\n\n- Credentials were reused from a service that suffered a breach\n- An API key was committed to a public repository\n- A former team member retained access after leaving","id":"DOC-SEC-001:50fa532aa23b:1","metadata":{"applies_to":"All plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"security","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":1,"content_sha256":"50fa532aa23b932d2aa7250a85eb6d758f9a997bd4a063301b133d4081453a67","doc_id":"DOC-SEC-001","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Common causes","title":"Responding to a suspected account compromise"}},{"document":"Title: Responding to a suspected account compromise\nApplies to: All plans\nSection: Resolution\n\n1. Revoke all API keys for the affected account immediately. This is disruptive and it is the correct first action.\n2. Force a password reset and terminate active sessions for the affected users from the team members page.\n3. Review the audit log for the period in question, filtering by the affected user, and record anything unexpected before it ages out.\n4. Enable multi-factor authentication for all users if it is not already mandatory for the organisation.","id":"DOC-SEC-001:50fa532aa23b:2","metadata":{"applies_to":"All plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"security","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":2,"content_sha256":"50fa532aa23b932d2aa7250a85eb6d758f9a997bd4a063301b133d4081453a67","doc_id":"DOC-SEC-001","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Resolution","title":"Responding to a suspected account compromise"}},{"document":"Title: Responding to a suspected account compromise\nApplies to: All plans\nSection: Notes\n\nAudit logs are retained for ninety days on Business plans and one year on Enterprise. Export them promptly during an investigation.","id":"DOC-SEC-001:50fa532aa23b:3","metadata":{"applies_to":"All plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"security","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":3,"content_sha256":"50fa532aa23b932d2aa7250a85eb6d758f9a997bd4a063301b133d4081453a67","doc_id":"DOC-SEC-001","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Notes","title":"Responding to a suspected account compromise"}},{"document":"Title: Handling exposed secrets and credential rotation\nApplies to: All plans\nSection: Symptoms\n\n- A key has been committed to a repository\n- A secret appears in application logs\n- A third party has reported finding a credential","id":"DOC-SEC-002:3311d2da9326:0","metadata":{"applies_to":"All plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"security","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":0,"content_sha256":"3311d2da93269b721f21365b3912199feb6232ae62d3da86e10084e4752e75be","doc_id":"DOC-SEC-002","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Symptoms","title":"Handling exposed secrets and credential rotation"}},{"document":"Title: Handling exposed secrets and credential rotation\nApplies to: All plans\nSection: Common causes\n\n- Configuration was committed rather than referenced from the environment\n- The application prints its configuration during startup\n- A key was shared in a support ticket or a chat message","id":"DOC-SEC-002:3311d2da9326:1","metadata":{"applies_to":"All plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"security","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":1,"content_sha256":"3311d2da93269b721f21365b3912199feb6232ae62d3da86e10084e4752e75be","doc_id":"DOC-SEC-002","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Common causes","title":"Handling exposed secrets and credential rotation"}},{"document":"Title: Handling exposed secrets and credential rotation\nApplies to: All plans\nSection: Resolution\n\n1. Revoke the exposed credential first. Removing it from the repository does not help, because it remains in the history.\n2. Issue a replacement with the narrowest scope that still works, rather than recreating the original permissions by default.\n3. Search the audit log for use of the exposed credential from unfamiliar addresses during the exposure window.\n4. Add secret scanning to your pipeline so that the next occurrence is caught before it reaches a remote branch.","id":"DOC-SEC-002:3311d2da9326:2","metadata":{"applies_to":"All plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"security","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":2,"content_sha256":"3311d2da93269b721f21365b3912199feb6232ae62d3da86e10084e4752e75be","doc_id":"DOC-SEC-002","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Resolution","title":"Handling exposed secrets and credential rotation"}},{"document":"Title: Handling exposed secrets and credential rotation\nApplies to: All plans\nSection: Notes\n\nNever send a live credential to support. Support will never ask for one, and any credential shared in a ticket must be treated as exposed.","id":"DOC-SEC-002:3311d2da9326:3","metadata":{"applies_to":"All plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"security","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":3,"content_sha256":"3311d2da93269b721f21365b3912199feb6232ae62d3da86e10084e4752e75be","doc_id":"DOC-SEC-002","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Notes","title":"Handling exposed secrets and credential rotation"}},{"document":"Title: Audit logging and compliance evidence\nApplies to: Business and Enterprise plans\nSection: Symptoms\n\n- An auditor has requested access records\n- An event that should be logged cannot be found\n- Log retention is shorter than a policy requires","id":"DOC-SEC-003:ab0a4cc5ba55:0","metadata":{"applies_to":"Business and Enterprise plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"security","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":0,"content_sha256":"ab0a4cc5ba55b17a33f734578fd130a77c3b83cec06c226de185a36cfa1352ac","doc_id":"DOC-SEC-003","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Symptoms","title":"Audit logging and compliance evidence"}},{"document":"Title: Audit logging and compliance evidence\nApplies to: Business and Enterprise plans\nSection: Common causes\n\n- The event predates the retention window\n- The event type is not covered by the audit log\n- The organisation is on a plan with shorter retention","id":"DOC-SEC-003:ab0a4cc5ba55:1","metadata":{"applies_to":"Business and Enterprise plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"security","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":1,"content_sha256":"ab0a4cc5ba55b17a33f734578fd130a77c3b83cec06c226de185a36cfa1352ac","doc_id":"DOC-SEC-003","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Common causes","title":"Audit logging and compliance evidence"}},{"document":"Title: Audit logging and compliance evidence\nApplies to: Business and Enterprise plans\nSection: Resolution\n\n1. Filter the audit log by actor, resource and date range. Every administrative action carries the user, the address and the outcome.\n2. Export the relevant period to object storage for anything needed beyond the retention window. Exports are not subject to retention limits.\n3. Configure continuous export to your own storage if a policy requires retention longer than the plan provides.\n4. Note that read access to resources is not logged on Business plans, only administrative and configuration changes.","id":"DOC-SEC-003:ab0a4cc5ba55:2","metadata":{"applies_to":"Business and Enterprise plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"security","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":2,"content_sha256":"ab0a4cc5ba55b17a33f734578fd130a77c3b83cec06c226de185a36cfa1352ac","doc_id":"DOC-SEC-003","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Resolution","title":"Audit logging and compliance evidence"}},{"document":"Title: Audit logging and compliance evidence\nApplies to: Business and Enterprise plans\nSection: Notes\n\nAudit log exports are themselves audited, including the fields selected and the destination.","id":"DOC-SEC-003:ab0a4cc5ba55:3","metadata":{"applies_to":"Business and Enterprise plans","approval_status":"approved","approval_status_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","article_version":"capstone-1.0","category":"security","chunk_count":4,"chunk_index":3,"content_sha256":"ab0a4cc5ba55b17a33f734578fd130a77c3b83cec06c226de185a36cfa1352ac","doc_id":"DOC-SEC-003","metadata_owner":"CloudServe capstone project maintainer","metadata_source":"Project-authored capstone metadata overlay in data/kb/metadata_manifest.json for the supplied assignment corpus; demo status scenarios were transcribed from its synthetic fixture fields and reviewed under the capstone-only procedure","review_interval_days":365,"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10","section":"Notes","title":"Audit logging and compliance evidence"}}]␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀