␀␀z4Learning rate multiplier for Reinforcement Learning.rÄ
␀␀z0Optional. Adapter size for Reinforcement Tuning.r¿
␀␀zMOptional. Number of different responses to generate per prompt during tuning.Úsamples_per_promptz’Optional. Batch size for the tuning job. How many prompts to process at a train step. If not set, the batch size will be determined automatically.rÀ
␀␀z¼Optional. How often at steps to evaluate the tuning job during training. If not set, evel will be run per epoch. `total_steps = epoch_count * samples_per_prompt / total_prompts_in_dataset`Úevaluate_intervalzÃOptional. How often at steps to save checkpoints during training. If not set, one checkpoint per epoch will be set. ```total_steps = epoch_count * samples_per_prompt / total_prompts_in_dataset```Úcheckpoint_intervalzPOptional. The maximum number of tokens to generate per prompt. Default to 32768.r•␀␀a␀␀Indicates the maximum thinking depth during tuning. Starting from Gemini 3.5 models, the old thinking_budget will no longer be supported and will result in a user error if set. Instead, users should use the thinking_level parameter to control the maximum thinking depth.rþ␀␀zÙOptional. The thinking budget for the tuning job to optimize for (Gemini 2.5 only). * -1 means dynamic thinking * 0 means no thinking * > 0 means thinking budget in tokens If not set, default to -1 (dynamic thinking).rý␀␀zSOptional. Number of steps for the tuning job (mutually exclusive with epoch_count).Ú
